---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const [muscles, exercises, routines] = await Promise.all([
  getCollection('muscles'),
  getCollection('exercises'),
  getCollection('routines'),
]);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Understanding stiff knees"
  description="A general educational reference on knee stiffness: how the joint works, which muscles are involved, and the movements commonly used to address them."
>
  <h1>Why is my knee stiff?</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A general reference on how the knee works, which muscles govern how freely it moves, and the
    movements commonly used to address them — drawn from clinical range-of-motion work, yoga,
    Pilates, and tai chi.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <h2>This cannot assess your knee</h2>
    <p>
      Everything here is general information. It does not know anything about your knee and
      cannot tell you what is wrong with it — that is what a clinician or physiotherapist is
      for. Some knee symptoms need looking at rather than stretching:
      <a href="/safety/">read which ones first</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Start here</h2>
    <ul class="grid">
      <li>
        <a class="card stack" href="/understanding/">
          <h3>Understanding stiffness</h3>
          <p>
            What the knee actually does, the six different physical reasons it stiffens, and how
            much movement daily life needs.
          </p>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="card stack" href="/muscles/">
          <h3>Muscles &amp; structures</h3>
          <p>
            {muscles.length} muscles and structures, what each does at the knee, and how it
            contributes when tight, weak, or switched off.
          </p>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="card stack" href="/exercises/">
          <h3>Exercise library</h3>
          <p>
            {exercises.length} movements across four traditions, filterable by muscle, goal,
            difficulty, and what equipment you have.
          </p>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="card stack" href="/routines/">
          <h3>Routines</h3>
          <p>{routines.length} ready-made sequences, with the reasoning behind their order.</p>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>One thing worth knowing up front</h2>
    <p>
      A stiff-feeling knee is frequently not a knee problem. The hip and the ankle both change
      what the knee has to do, and restriction at either one gets felt at the joint in between.
      That is why this reference spends as much time on <a href="/muscles/iliopsoas/">hip
      flexors</a>, <a href="/muscles/gluteus-medius/">gluteal muscles</a>, and
      <a href="/muscles/soleus/">the calf</a> as it does on the knee itself.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
